<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply raised in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply raised in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank said it added liquidity to the money market in the week to June 2 to offset the tightening effect of a rise in note circulation and and a rise in financial institutions deposits with the bank.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   446.95 (+  0.26)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  19.39 (+  0.72)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	 114.86 (+  0.68)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   475.25 (+  0.55)</p>
<p> Current account account in francs   8.85 (+  4.24)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
